  {
   "duty_id": "MP-0",
   "duty": "ED26-P15-CH-product-measures-C013 (partial): The full treatment promised by the declared status proved=annex:p15.absolute-iterated-series is not supplied. The series half of the proof connects the corollary's sums to Fubini's integrals only through two bare assertions. The first is 'The assumed sum is the first iterated absolute integral, because integration with respect to kappa is summation' (handbook/annex/p15/product-measures.tex 514-515). The second is 'counting-measure integration of that integrable section equals the sum' (519-521). Neither identity is derived in this proof or established anywhere on the route: the integral against counting measure on N+ of a nonnegative g equals the sum of g(n), and the signed version holds for an absolutely summable section. The closest result, thm:p15-expectation-law-integral (handbook/parts/p15/integration-expectation.tex 324-348), gives the sum formula only for countable atomic probability spaces. Three identifications are therefore unwritten: the hypothesis sum of the integrals of |f_n| with Fubini's premise, H with the section absolute integral (516-518), and S with Fubini's second section-integral function (522-523). All other parts of C013 (the Tonelli criterion at 499-504, product measurability of F, the absolute-convergence bound, integrability of each f_n) are written.",
   "verdict": "partial",
   "evidence": [
    {
     "path": "handbook/annex/p15/product-measures.tex",
     "line_start": 497,
     "line_end": 535,
     "label": "annex:p15.absolute-iterated-series"
    }
   ],
   "gap": "Supply the full treatment promised by proved=annex:p15.absolute-iterated-series: derive that for counting measure kappa on N+ the integral of a nonnegative g equals sum_n g(n), and that for an absolutely summable real section the signed kappa-integral equals the sum; then use these to identify the hypothesis sum_n int|f_n| dnu with Fubini's first iterated absolute integral (handbook/annex/p15/product-measures.tex lines 514-515, bare assertion 'integration with respect to kappa is summation'), H with the section absolute integral (516-518), and S with Fubini's second section-integral function (519-523, bare assertion 'counting-measure integration of that integrable section equals the sum'). No route result supplies these identities; thm:p15-expectation-law-integral covers only countable atomic probability spaces."
